  "project_description": "AIDmi (AI, describe my image!) adds a CKEditor 5 toolbar button and a per-image sidebar action that use the Drupal AI module's vision-capable chat providers to generate Section 508 / WCAG-oriented alternative text and optional visible <figcaption> captions for images embedded in rich-text content. It works on both inline `<img>` uploads and `drupal-media` image embeds. The toolbar button runs a bulk sweep over every image in the editor body (optionally sending the surrounding article text as context so descriptions match the page), loads results into a review dialog where the editor picks AI-suggested or decorative alt text per image, and writes the chosen values back into the CKEditor content (setting alt and, for captions, restructuring the asset as an HTML figure with a figcaption). The per-image button next to the core Alternative Text field triggers a focused single-image evaluation. Model selection, the base prompt, the context toggle, and the caption toggle are configured at /admin/config/services/aidmi; provider/API-key authentication is delegated entirely to the Drupal AI module and the Key module, so AIDmi never stores credentials itself. Requires the ai and key modules and a configured vision-capable AI provider.",
